------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changes made in this conversion (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b)):

  - The checkpoint's text model, DSpark drafter (mtp.safetensors) and vision tower
    were converted into one Infernix v3 artifact, Inkling-2-Mini-Infernix.infernix,
    with the inkling2_mini recipe of Infernix's tools.convert.
  - The NVFP4 and MXFP8 routed experts keep their codes and scales unchanged,
    regrouped into one record per expert. Each NVFP4 expert also stores the multiplier
    fl32(amax / denominator), beside the checkpoint's amax and denominator.
  - BF16 and FP32 tensors keep their values. Some are reordered without changing a
    value: the static convolutions (lag-major) and the looped layers' cross-pass
    queries.
  - The token embedding, output head and DSpark Markov embedding keep the rows of the
    200,058 assigned tokens; the checkpoint's 966 padding rows, which no token id can
    reach, are not stored.
  - DSpark's Fold and fold_bias are derived from the output head and hidden_out, which
    is not stored. The vision class row is derived as the BF16 sum of class_embedding
    and cls_position_embedding.
  - Added proposal/token_rank, an ordering of the vocabulary (below).
  - Tokenizer, chat template, generation and processor configs: stored unchanged as
    artifact resources.
  - README.md, config.json (metadata only) and the conversion report added.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Token ranking (proposal/token_rank):

The ranking orders the vocabulary by Inkling 2 Mini's own top prediction at each
assistant position of a chat corpus, built from the datasets below. The artifact
stores only the resulting order of token ids. It contains no text from any dataset.
The datasets were selected, filtered, tokenized and counted by Infernix's
tools/freq_corpus; they are not redistributed here.

